  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{R}=\\{(1,2),(2,3),(3,3)\\}$ be a relation defined on the set $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$. Then the minimum number of elements, needed to be added in R so that R becomes an equivalence relation, is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VwgWe",
      "text": "$10$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZZKDm",
      "text": "$7$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zJ3oQ",
      "text": "$8$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "A2mTY",
      "text": "$9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$A=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\n\nFor relation to be reflexive\n$\\mathrm{R}=\\{(1,2),(2,3),(3,3)\\}$\n\nMinimum elements added will be\n$(1,1),(2,2),(4,4)(2,1)(3,2)(3,2)(3,1)(1,3)$\n$\\therefore$ Minimum number of elements $=7$",
    "image": null
  },
